From 98b42babd75d8555d7220100f9cd29b7656397a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mojavemesa-lgtm <252102886+mojavemesa-lgtm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:32:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/16] power: supply: qcom_smbx: Enable the periodic AICL
 rerun on SMB2

Mainline leaves USBIN_AICL_PERIODIC_RERUN_EN (USBIN_AICL_OPTIONS_CFG,
0x1380 bit 4) off, and the AICL rerun time (0x1661) at its default. The
downstream OnePlus driver enables the periodic rerun with the shortest
interval.

Without it the hardware AICL (automatic input current limit) only ever
steps the input limit down when VBUS dips (a weak power bank, a long
cable) and never tries again. The limit ratchets down to a few tens of
milliamps and charging stops altogether; a power bank then switches
itself off because the load is too small.

Enable the periodic rerun and set the rerun time field to 0 (shortest),
as downstream does.

Tested on a OnePlus 6T (fajita) with an Anker power bank: 0x1380 reads
back 0x57 after boot, and the phone kept charging at 1.05 - 1.1 A for
more than 10 minutes instead of ratcheting down.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index 01f98287c..e8a66ac35 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -134,6 +134,9 @@ enum smb_generation {
 #define USBIN_HV_COLLAPSE_RESPONSE_BIT			BIT(1)
 #define USBIN_LV_COLLAPSE_RESPONSE_BIT			BIT(0)
 
+#define AICL_RERUN_TIME_CFG				0x661
+#define AICL_RERUN_TIME_MASK				GENMASK(1, 0)
+
 // FIXME: drop these and their programming, no need to set min to 4.3v
 #define USBIN_5V_AICL_THRESHOLD_CFG			0x381
 #define USBIN_5V_AICL_THRESHOLD_CFG_MASK		GENMASK(2, 0)
@@ -828,6 +831,16 @@ static const struct smb_init_register smb2_init_seq[] = {
 	  .val = 0 },
 	/* Configure VBUS for software control */
 	{ .addr = OTG_CFG, .mask = OTG_EN_SRC_CFG_BIT, .val = 0 },
+	/*
+	 * Re-run AICL periodically (shortest interval), as the downstream
+	 * driver does. Without it the hardware AICL only ever steps the input
+	 * limit down on VBUS dips (weak power banks, long cables) and never
+	 * recovers, until charging stops altogether.
+	 */
+	{ .addr = USBIN_AICL_OPTIONS_CFG,
+	  .mask = USBIN_AICL_PERIODIC_RERUN_EN_BIT,
+	  .val = USBIN_AICL_PERIODIC_RERUN_EN_BIT },
+	{ .addr = AICL_RERUN_TIME_CFG, .mask = AICL_RERUN_TIME_MASK, .val = 0 },
 	/*
 	 * Use VBAT to determine the recharge threshold when battery is full
 	 * rather than the state of charge.
